  "title": "A uniform two-term expansion for the lane-merging gap near capacity",
  "batch_label": "新WIN-1批次",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For integers m>=1 and 0<=k<=2m-1, let E_{m,k}=G_{m,k}/binom(2m-1,k), where G_{m,k}=sum_{i=0}^k binom(2m-1,i) if k<m, and G_{m,k}=sum_{i=0}^{2m-2-k} binom(2m-1,i)+(k-m+1)binom(2m,k+1) if k>=m, with a sum with negative upper endpoint equal to zero. Define x_+=max(x,0), erfc(t)=(2/sqrt(pi))*integral_t^infinity exp(-u^2)du, H(x)=(sqrt(pi)/2)exp(x^2)erfc(|x|), F0(x)=H(x)+2x_+, and F1(x,delta)=(2delta+1)xH(x)+delta+1-2x_+^2 for real x and -1<delta<=0. For every real A>0 there exist a finite C_A>=0 and an integer M_A>=1 such that for every integer m>=M_A and every real |x|<=A, k=m+floor(x sqrt(m)) is admissible and |E_{m,k}-sqrt(m)F0(x)-F1(x,delta_m(x))|<=C_A/sqrt(m), where delta_m(x)=floor(x sqrt(m))-x sqrt(m). This includes x=0, all floor jumps, and m-dependent real x. Explicit nonoptimized C_A and M_A are given in equations (6), (11), (13), (18), and (19) of evidence/research-proof.md. No growing-window extension is claimed.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
